          code("action"), " drift_tape applies the tape offsets to this logger or site, drift_manual applies ", code("value"), " at the start and ", code("value_end"), " at the end, ",
          "drift_none never corrects it, drift_keep keeps a large tape offset as it is; ", code("year"), " limits a drift row to one year. Removals are applied with the limits, drift after the tape checks."), editUI("period")),
        tabPanel("Readings in the air", p(class = "dim", "Runs at the start or end of a deployment where the logger read almost no water: launched before it went in, or left logging after it came out. They are flagged (or dropped, if Trim readings in the air is on under Settings). Select runs to drop them for good; each becomes a removal of whole records under Corrections over a period."),
                 DTOutput("qa_air"),
                 div(class = "panel-x editor-only", fluidRow(column(6, textInput("qa_reason", "Reason", "logging in the air before or after deployment", width = "100%")), column(3, textInput("qa_author", "Initials", width = "100%"))),
                     div(class = "btnrow", actionButton("qa_drop", "Drop the selected runs", class = "btn-danger")))),
        tabPanel("Out of water", p(class = "dim", "Retrievals, downloads or data errors when the sensor was not in the water. Pressure, depth and elevation are removed for the period; ", code("cause"), " is retrieval, download, data error or other."), editUI("oow")))),

    ovid_tool("Clock checks", value = "Clock", icon = "clock",
      page_head("Clock checks", paste0("Every time stamp is moved to ", zone_text(BASE_OFFSET), " (the time zone in Settings) without daylight saving. A zone set by hand for one file (Raw files) wins; then the zone the file states (HOBOware: GMT-06:00); then the time-zone table below; anything else is taken as ", zone_text(BASE_OFFSET), ". Shift a span of one logger under Clock corrections.")),
      h4("Files and the zone they were read in"), DTOutput("ck_files"),
      h4("Time-zone table"), p(class = "dim", "Sets the zone for many files at once, for files that do not state one (Solinst, or a CSV exported without a zone). Fill in any of ",
        code("serial"), ", ", code("model"), " (part of the name, e.g. LT_EDGE or U20), ", code("file_pattern"), " (a folder or part of the path, e.g. 2019/) and ",
        code("start"), "/", code("end"), " (the file's first reading falls in this span); blank matches anything. ", code("offset_hours"), " is the clock's offset from UTC, e.g. -6. The first matching row wins, so put one-logger rows above whole-year rows."), editUI("tzt"),
      h4("Clock corrections"), p(class = "dim", code("shift_minutes"), " moves the readings of ", code("serial"), " between ", code("start"), " and ", code("end"), " (blank = all). ", code("mode"), " drift spreads a clock error found at download over the span instead: no shift at the start, ", code("shift_minutes"), " at the end."), editUI("time")),

    convert_tool(), reference_tool("WLR"),
    ovid_tool("Settings", value = "Settings", icon = "sliders", rail = FALSE,
